(4828564, 697084, 93946, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments, very helpful.  I hope to learn a lot here.  It is a bit intimidating with all the talent on these pages.   I did notice this image was grainy, just after turned to jpeg at a few minutes to 12p- so no time to change.  Didn''t expect it to do this well!</td>', 'Thanks for the comments, very helpful.  I hope to learn a lot here.  It is a bit intimidating with all the talent on these pages.   I did notice this image was grainy, just after turned to jpeg at a few minutes to 12p- so no time to change.  Didn''t expect it to do this well!', '2008-07-16 11:12:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4828588, 696492, 67697, '<td valign="top">lol you know, I never see spirits in photos (but I would like to!) and i don''t see one here.  Someone usually has to draw big arrows and circles to point it out to me lol.  This is a beautiful shot and you did a wonderful job capturing the rustic nature of the piece.  Congrats on your new 3rd PB!</td>', 'lol you know, I never see spirits in photos (but I would like to!) and i don''t see one here.  Someone usually has to draw big arrows and circles to point it out to me lol.  This is a beautiful shot and you did a wonderful job capturing the rustic nature of the piece.  Congrats on your new 3rd PB!', '2008-07-16 11:16:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4828604, 695621, 93946, '<td valign="top">Not sure how people vote yet, being new here, but it seems to me an image that is in focus, nicely composed and meets challenge (such as yours) should rate at LEAST 5, despite if one likes it personally or not.   I think if a person votes 4 or less they should be required to comment on why, so we can learn from it.</td>', 'Not sure how people vote yet, being new here, but it seems to me an image that is in focus, nicely composed and meets challenge (such as yours) should rate at LEAST 5, despite if one likes it personally or not.   I think if a person votes 4 or less they should be required to comment on why, so we can learn from it.', '2008-07-16 11:19:37.000000', NULL, 0),
