(4828808, 695857, 77287, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yospiff:</b></div><hr/><i> Fascinating image. I''d like to know what the story is here. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Hi.<br/> <br/>This was at a music festival in the North West of England called ''Beat-Herder''.<br/>As is traditional with UK festivals it rained a lot and the whole place turned into a mud bath.<br/>I saw this Sinatra type character making his way through the rain towards the main stage.<br/>He was covered in mud and still had the price label hanging from the back of his hat (which you can just see).<br/>You can see the conditions and the label here........<br/> <br/><a href="//s269.photobucket.com/albums/jj51/TacTZilla/?action=view&amp;current=Weathered2.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//s269.photobucket.com/albums/jj51/TacTZilla/?action=view&amp;current=Weathered2.jpg</a> <br/> <br/>I called it ''probably'' because there used to be a Carlsberg advertising campaign. ''Carlsberg - Probably the best lager in the world.''<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Bob<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by yospiff: Fascinating image. I''d like to know what the story is here.  Hi. This was at a music festival in the North West of England called ''Beat-Herder''.As is traditional with UK festivals it rained a lot and the whole place turned into a mud bath.I saw this Sinatra type character making his way through the rain towards the main stage.He was covered in mud and still had the price label hanging from the back of his hat (which you can just see).You can see the conditions and the label here........ //s269.photobucket.com/albums/jj51/TacTZilla/?action=view&current=Weathered2.jpg  I called it ''probably'' because there used to be a Carlsberg advertising campaign. ''Carlsberg - Probably the best lager in the world.'' CheersBob', '2008-07-16 12:23:48.000000', NULL, 0),
