(4846142, 696901, 54645, '<td valign="top">This was one of my favorites in the challenge. I would have given it an 8 if I could. I think if the post was more vertical it would have been a top 10, but that was out of your control. To my favorites.<br/>Go Jokers!</td>', 'This was one of my favorites in the challenge. I would have given it an 8 if I could. I think if the post was more vertical it would have been a top 10, but that was out of your control. To my favorites.Go Jokers!', '2008-07-27 01:17:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4850032, 696213, 41337, '<td valign="top">Judging by your edit and your title I am going to assume the texture of the rock face is what you found of interest. If so getting closer would have helped here, IMO. By zooming out you make this rock face appear more flat and you lose the sense of the texture and the depth it has. Other than that this is a pretty compent shot. In terms of your PP work I would get ride of those dark halos that your edit produced. If you have photoshop use the stamp tool for this. Just set it to "lighen" mode and then on a duplicate layer sample an area right underneath the dark halo and then paint over it and it should disappear. Just FYI, if you have a white halo you want to remove just change the mode to "darken" instead.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-29 20:16:44.</i></td>', 'Judging by your edit and your title I am going to assume the texture of the rock face is what you found of interest. If so getting closer would have helped here, IMO. By zooming out you make this rock face appear more flat and you lose the sense of the texture and the depth it has. Other than that this is a pretty compent shot. In terms of your PP work I would get ride of those dark halos that your edit produced. If you have photoshop use the stamp tool for this. Just set it to "lighen" mode and then on a duplicate layer sample an area right underneath the dark halo and then paint over it and it should disappear. Just FYI, if you have a white halo you want to remove just change the mode to "darken" instead.', '2008-07-29 21:15:51.000000', '2008-07-29 21:16:44.000000', 0),
(4850067, 696213, 92643, '<td valign="top">great colors, but I agree with yanko about the texture of the rock.</td>', 'great colors, but I agree with yanko about the texture of the rock.', '2008-07-29 21:35:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4850784, 696525, 41337, '<td valign="top">You showed the challenge theme well but it''s not compelling enough and lacks the wow factor. DPC loves extremes whether it be an extreme close up or an extreme grunge effect. Focus on one aspect you think is most important and do everything you can (ex composition, lighting, dof) to enhance it. In this case you could really show off how each of the three weathered differently by going with a closer and tighter crop. Maybe even move the buoy, rope and chain around so that you can get all three in a more pleasing/dynamic arrangement. You had it right in the thread. Keep it simple.</td>', 'You showed the challenge theme well but it''s not compelling enough and lacks the wow factor. DPC loves extremes whether it be an extreme close up or an extreme grunge effect. Focus on one aspect you think is most important and do everything you can (ex composition, lighting, dof) to enhance it. In this case you could really show off how each of the three weathered differently by going with a closer and tighter crop. Maybe even move the buoy, rope and chain around so that you can get all three in a more pleasing/dynamic arrangement. You had it right in the thread. Keep it simple.', '2008-07-30 02:46:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4853077, 697029, 91496, '<td valign="top">No comments during challenge.  I hate when I see (or get) that!  Nice shot.  The crop and the angle are great.  The textures are nice and B&amp;W was a good pick to highlight them.  The blown out sky detracts somewhat.</td>', 'No comments during challenge.  I hate when I see (or get) that!  Nice shot.  The crop and the angle are great.  The textures are nice and B&W was a good pick to highlight them.  The blown out sky detracts somewhat.', '2008-07-31 10:24:57.000000', NULL, 0),
